# tests/artifact-fixtures/artifact-blank-path-fixture.ttl
#
# O3's fixture (spec §7): a shape whose sh:path is a BLANK NODE holding a property-path
# expression, hiding one owned term behind an RDF list. The sole real occurrence of this
# construct in the tree is vocab/shapes/doc-governance-shapes.ttl (see § the docgov row of
# spec §2.3); this fixture makes the case testable in isolation and permanently.
#
# It names BOTH a DECLARED owned term (etkl:SemanticDataContract) and an UNDECLARED one
# (etkl:NoSuchPathTermAnywhere). Without the declared one the test would pass against a
# derivation that demands everything it sees — the selectivity trap R135 Task 2 measured.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY INVALID under the declaration membrane. It lives in
# tests/artifact-fixtures/ because the artifact population is EVERY tracked .ttl, so a
# fixture anywhere else would join its own population and turn the corpus permanently red.
# `test_the_fixtures_are_not_in_the_population` pins that carve-out.
#
# © 2026 François Rosselet · CC-BY-4.0
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#> .

<urn:iladub:fixture:blank-path> a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path [ sh:alternativePath ( etkl:SemanticDataContract etkl:NoSuchPathTermAnywhere ) ] ;
    ] .
